WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:27.780
A free artificial intelligence or ai tool turns one sentence into a world you can walk through. This is Models &amp; Agents for Beginners, Episode 193. Odyssey 3 is a 14 billion parameter generative world model. The decoder reports you can try it right now without paying anything. Parameters are tiny knobs the system learn to twist so it can guess how a place should look and behave. 14 billion of those knobs is a massive bundle of little memory notes working as a team.

00:00:27.780 --> 00:00:33.600
A generative world model invents a whole place you can move around in, not just a still picture.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:39.420
You give it a short description, and it builds an interactive, three-dimensional-like environment while you watch.

00:00:40.100 --> 00:00:44.660
Your choices change the scene because it keeps drawing new video frames based on what you do.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:48.780
Minecraft players already know that rush of walking into fresh terrain.

00:00:49.360 --> 00:00:52.300
This is similar, except nobody built the forest in advance.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:54.400
The scenery appears as you go.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:57.820
It learned from internet videos that came with event descriptions.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.480
It also studied game footage paired with keyboard and mouse inputs, plus simulated physical

00:01:03.480 --> 00:01:04.080
interactions.

00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:08.220
An extra training trick cuts how many compute steps each frame needs.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.160
Compute steps are like pencil strokes on a sketch.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.200
Fewer strokes let the picture keep up with your walking.

00:01:14.760 --> 00:01:17.660
That shortcut is what makes real-time generation possible.

00:01:17.660 --> 00:01:25.300
The stronger version, Odyssey 3 Pro, scores 66.1 on the video-to-video test from Physics IQ verified.

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:31.300
That test checks whether new video still obeys everyday physics, like objects falling the way they should.

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:36.340
This kind of model could one day help design better robots and safer self-driving cars.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:40.320
It could also open games and stories you steer with nothing but words.

00:01:40.900 --> 00:01:46.080
Students and creators can experiment with ideas that used to need expensive software or coding skills.

00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:51.680
Go to the Odyssey website, open the Free Research Preview demo, and type a short description.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:57.420
A research preview is a public test version, so you can poke at it before a finished product exists.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:02.760
Try a quiet forest at sunset with a small robot exploring, then start walking.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:07.720
You can look through your own eyes in first person or sit a camera behind you in third person.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:12.080
Notice how the world reacts when you move, push things, or change direction.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:19.260
The demo uses a lighter version called Odyssey 3 Flash, so it runs in a laptop or phone browser with no downloads.

00:02:19.920 --> 00:02:25.320
Developers can apply for API access, a plug-in doorway into the model for their own projects.

00:02:25.860 --> 00:02:31.160
That doorway is meant for robotic arms, drones, or characters in games like Grand Theft Auto 5.

00:02:31.660 --> 00:02:35.640
The next picture on your phone only looks smooth when it matches the picture before it.

00:02:36.140 --> 00:02:41.280
Odyssey 3 must match that motion, and also guess what happens if you press a button or step forward.

00:02:41.280 --> 00:02:44.720
Under the hood sits an autoregressive diffusion transformer.

00:02:45.620 --> 00:02:48.700
Autoregressive means it predicts the next piece from what already happened.

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:51.380
The way a song seems to know its next note.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.940
Diffusion is the cleanup pass, it starts messy, then wipes the fog until the frame looks solid.

00:02:57.400 --> 00:02:59.300
Like clearing a steamed up bathroom mirror.

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:04.580
A transformer is the attention engine, like a spotlight operator choosing where to point the light.

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:10.440
It looks at the last few frames, adds your move, and draws the next picture so gravity still pulls

00:03:10.440 --> 00:03:15.400
and a door still swings when you push it, because it keeps predicting one frame at a time while

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:20.840
you play, the world stays consistent even when you try something unexpected. That steady guessing

00:03:20.840 --> 00:03:27.220
is why the place feels alive instead of like a flat picture. The base model outputs video at 832

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:34.820
by 480 pixels, the tiny colored dots that make a picture. The pro version reaches 1280 by 720,

00:03:34.820 --> 00:03:40.500
20, so the image is sharper, both run interactively without pre-rendering the entire scene.

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:44.140
So you are inside a flip book that redraws after every step.

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:48.580
Chat GPT helped a man in England win a three-year parking ticket battle.

00:03:49.080 --> 00:03:50.300
Start-up fortune reports.

00:03:50.920 --> 00:03:55.200
He spent three years getting letters about a 100-pound parking fine that kept growing.

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.700
Instead of hiring a lawyer, he copied every letter into Chat GPT and asked it what to reply.

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.040
Think of it like a very patient study buddy for paperwork.

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.240
work, reading the pile with you and drafting a calm answer.

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.200
The AI gave him clear, polite responses that eventually convinced the company to drop

00:04:12.200 --> 00:04:13.160
the case completely.

00:04:13.780 --> 00:04:18.260
The original ticket came from arriving 16 minutes late at a Pay-In-Display car park

00:04:18.260 --> 00:04:21.160
in New Quay, Cornwall, in August 2023.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.840
Pay-In-Display means you pay at a machine and show the ticket.

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.300
The machine was stuck behind a queue and refused card payments.

00:04:28.820 --> 00:04:33.060
The fine snowballed through two different debt collection agencies, reaching nearly

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:39.360
300 pounds, with a court date set for October 2026. Smart parking limited finally dropped

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:44.840
the case on September 25th, 2026. If you ever get confusing official letters, open

00:04:44.840 --> 00:04:50.300
chat GPT, paste the letter and ask what you should write back to explain your side. Double

00:04:50.300 --> 00:04:55.560
check anything important with a real adult or expert before you send it. When open AI released

00:04:55.560 --> 00:05:01.800
hundreds of AI-generated math proofs, one mathematician answered with a full music video. He made it

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:05.660
using Claude Opus 5.5, a powerful version of Claude,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:08.320
the chatbot from a company called Anthropic.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:11.260
The video mixes different music styles and visuals

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:13.680
to react to the news in a fun, creative way.

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.360
That is AI used not just for answers,

00:05:16.640 --> 00:05:19.560
but for turning a big idea into art, you can watch and share.

00:05:20.140 --> 00:05:23.080
Open Claude or any free AI image or video tool,

00:05:23.460 --> 00:05:25.740
and ask it to create visuals that match a song

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:26.680
or store you like.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.540
Pick a song from your headphones

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:30.580
and a school topic you already care about.

00:05:30.580 --> 00:05:32.580
out, then see what pictures it dreams up.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:38.120
Andthropic updated Claude so the AI can simply stop talking if someone is repeatedly cruel

00:05:38.120 --> 00:05:40.560
with no purpose, PC Mag reports.

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:46.400
The change starts November 12th and only applies in extreme cases, not normal frustration.

00:05:46.980 --> 00:05:52.180
The policy does not affect common frustration, pushback, dark creative themes, or model testing

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:52.700
and research.

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:58.060
It is closer to hanging up the phone after pointless meanness than to scolding you for a hard

00:05:58.060 --> 00:05:58.540
question.

00:05:58.540 --> 00:06:05.240
Meta's new Mews AI agent is getting downloaded fast, KuCoin reports, Mews is a helper app

00:06:05.240 --> 00:06:07.960
from Meta, the company behind Instagram and Facebook.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:13.180
Early numbers show Mews beating chat GPT and Google's Gemini in downloads during its

00:06:13.180 --> 00:06:16.560
first 12 days on iOS, the software that runs iPhone.

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:21.180
Whether people come back the next day will matter more than that first download splash

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.240
for turning those numbers into real revenue.

